WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.340
If deleting a protein cannot reveal the pore, what experiment can?

2
00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:14.463
In 2011, Kawashima and colleagues removed both TMC1 and TMC2.

3
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:18.543
Hair cells lacking both had no conventional current.

4
00:00:18.543 --> 00:00:21.183
Putting back either gene restored it.

5
00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:25.023
That puts the TMC proteins in the pathway.

6
00:00:25.923 --> 00:00:30.283
But loss and rescue act on the whole product, so they cannot separate a pore from

7
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:31.283
its helpers.

8
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:36.383
The sharper test keeps the channel working, and changes one amino acid.

9
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:39.493
The Beethoven mouse carries such a change.

10
00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:44.433
Methionine 412 of mouse TMC1 becomes lysine.

11
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:51.163
In 2013, Pan and colleagues recorded from inner hair cells lacking Tmc2.

12
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.243
So every channel had to use TMC1.

13
00:00:55.183 --> 00:01:01.403
Predict. If TMC1 only delivered or anchored the channel, what would a point mutation

14
00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:02.403
change?

15
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:12.257
If only the delivery of normal channels changed, there would be fewer channels.

16
00:01:13.177 --> 00:01:14.997
A coupling defect would mean fewer open.

17
00:01:15.877 --> 00:01:17.457
Each open channel would be unchanged.

18
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.180
But the Beethoven channels let through less calcium.

19
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.360
That calcium result has been replicated.

20
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.300
Whether the single-channel current also shrinks is disputed.

21
00:01:30.183 --> 00:01:33.743
One residue in TMC1 changed which ions pass.

22
00:01:34.503 --> 00:01:36.303
A deletion can never show that.

23
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:40.497
But a partner beside the pore can also change what passes.

24
00:01:41.377 --> 00:01:43.017
So this rung narrows the candidates.

25
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.300
Next, change the channel while it works.

26
00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:52.940
In 2018, Pan and colleagues made TMC1 with single cysteine substitutions.

27
00:01:53.933 --> 00:01:57.953
Delivered into hair cells lacking both genes, they restored a current.

28
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:02.797
Then they added a reagent that cannot cross the membrane.

29
00:02:03.697 --> 00:02:05.157
It reacts with cysteine in water.

30
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.700
Predict. The current is already flowing when the reagent arrives.

31
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.260
If permeation changes, what does that rule out?

32
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.800
It rules out altered synthesis or delivery.

33
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.320
The current existed before the reagent was added.

34
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:32.373
A residue reached from outside, whose change alters which ions pass, points to a

35
00:02:32.373 --> 00:02:33.373
water-filled route.

36
00:02:33.973 --> 00:02:35.353
That is what a pore would provide.

37
00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:41.183
The cells still had their native partners, and a reachable residue may sit beside

38
00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:45.803
the pore. No purified mammalian TMC1 was tested alone.

39
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:53.933
Purified, truncated turtle TMC1 and budgerigar TMC2, in liposomes, responded to

40
00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:54.933
pressure.

41
00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:59.447
That supports force-gated activity in a reduced system.

42
00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:03.887
The proteins were not mammalian, and this was not a native complex.

43
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.290
Each rung ruled out a different alternative.

44
00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.450
None alone proves the pore.
